Open the Browser pane: pass `url` to open a browser tab at a URL (no dev server needed — use this for external sites, staging, docs, or your deployed app), OR pass `name` to start a dev server from .claude/launch.json.

Start a dev server by name from .claude/launch.json. If .claude/launch.json doesn't exist, create it first with this format:
{
  "version": "0.0.1",
  "configurations": [
    {
      "name": "<unique-name>",
      "runtimeExecutable": "<command>",
      "runtimeArgs": ["<args>"],
      "port": <port>
    }
  ]
}
Set "runtimeExecutable" to the command (e.g. "npm"), "runtimeArgs" to the arguments (e.g. ["run", "dev"]), and "port" to the server port. An optional "url" (http/https) opens the preview there instead of http://localhost:<port>. A localhost "url" must be just the server's origin — no path or query, matching the entry's port — for example "https://localhost:8443" or "http://app.localhost:3000"; to show a specific page, navigate after the preview opens. Non-localhost URLs may carry paths and are subject to the user's permission and the organization's browsing policy. A configuration with "url" and no command attaches to an already-running server. Only include servers you actually need to preview. Reuses the server if already running. ALWAYS use this instead of Bash for running servers. If the deliverable is already published as an Artifact, update the Artifact instead of starting a server to show it.

content.content:
OrcaSlicer opens message windows from hundreds of call sites. The JusPrin
view takes them (`docs/HLSD/orca-messages.md`). What was learned:

- **A window put off has lost its reason by the time it opens.**
  `GUI::show_error`, `GUI_App::show_dialog` and `GUI_App::push_notification`
  queue the window with `CallAfter` and return. The modal hook then sees a box
  with no caller on the stack. The message is taken at the top of each of the
  three functions instead, where the caller still is; a modal window opened at
  once is taken at the hook.
- **The reason has to be noted at the source.** A box's words do not say what
  it is about: "Connect ... failed!" names no device id, and the network
  plug-in's update message names none at all. The cause is noted by the code
  that knows it, and JusPrin's listeners of a finished slice or a failed
  upload run before OrcaSlicer's own, since the handler bound later runs
  first.
- **One window class has three uses.** `UnsavedChangesDialog` asks
  "Transfer or discard changes" on a profile switch, "<caption>: unsaved
  changes" before profiles are reloaded, and whether to copy one nozzle's
  settings to the other. The copy always has unsaved options, so the dirty
  state does not tell them apart; only the title does.
- **`UnsavedChangesDialog::ShowModal` can return without opening.** With
  "remember my choice" set it returns the remembered action before the modal
  hook is asked. The hook's answer of OK leaves the exit action undefined,
  which every caller reads as neither transfer nor save.
- **A profile switch can ask about another profile's edits.** A printer
  switch asks about the process or filament edits when the selected process
  or filament does not fit the new printer (`Tab::select_preset`, the printer
  branch), with the same "Transfer or discard changes" window. Installing a
  printer profile (`PresetBundle::apply_vendor_config`) reloads every
  profile and drops their edits without asking.
- **The answer of a switch is the switch's own Discard.** Answering OK lets
  `Tab::select_preset` drop the outgoing edits itself; the reload callers read
  no choice from an undefined action, so the edits are dropped first.
- **A page switch is refused with the notebook's own event.** Veto of
  `wxEVT_BOOKCTRL_PAGE_CHANGING` stops `SelectPageByName`, `select_tab` and the
  key that steps through pages alike, without a line in `MainFrame`.
- **A failed upload's entry never says it failed.** The upload's chat entry
  follows OrcaSlicer's progress notification (`PrintIssues/WorkFeed.cpp`).
  On an error the notification only changes the state it draws, not the text
  `for_each_notification` reads, so the entry stays running. The failure is in
  the upload queue's error event, which is why OrcaSlicer's error box about it
  is still shown, as a confirmation on the canvas.

### Application teardown can re-enter destroyed owners

----
#pragma once

// What OrcaSlicer tells the person while the JusPrin view is on screen.
//
// OrcaSlicer speaks in one of two ways. It opens a modal box in the same call
// that decided to speak, or it puts the message off: GUI::show_error,
// GUI_App::show_dialog and GUI_App::push_notification queue the box and
// return. JusPrin takes the message at the last point where its reason is
// still known. For a box opened at once that is the modal hook every dialog
// passes (Workspace/DialogListeners.hpp), because the code that asked is still
// running. For a message put off it is one line at the top of each of the
// three functions, which hands the message here while its caller is still on
// the stack.
//
// The reason is a cause, noted at the doors where work comes in: a printer's
// answer to a connection (Printers::record_connection_event), a printer's
// reply (push_notification is given the printer), the network plug-in's
// message (GUI_App::process_network_msg), a slice that ended in an error and a
// failed upload to a print host (JusPrin's listeners of those events, which
// run before OrcaSlicer's own). A person's click in OrcaSlicer's own menus has no cause.
//
// The rule at the hook, for a window no listener answered:
// - A file or folder picker, a window with fields, and a question with a
//   choice are the person's, and open as OrcaSlicer's.
// - A message with only OK is taken, unless another window is open over the
//   main one: a box then belongs with that window, where the person is looking.
// - "Transfer or discard changes", and the unsaved-changes question OrcaSlicer
//   asks before it reloads presets, are answered after a version of the
//   project is saved: the setting changes are dropped and the version keeps
//   them. When no version can be saved, nothing changes and the failure is
//   reported as unexpected.
// - JusPrin's own windows (OwnDialogs.hpp) are never taken.
//
// What becomes of a taken message is the view's: see MessageRoutes.hpp.
//
// GUI thread only.

#include <wx/string.h>

#include <functional>

